// THE ROYAL SEED POD (Corey, 13 October 2026) - Commune with it and it puts you at the foot of the
// Grand Tree. Bought from the Undertaker for Death tokens; nothing else in this build gives one.
//
// IT LIVES UNDER area_wilderness BECAUSE ITS SOURCE DOES, not because it is wilderness content. It
// is King Narnode's, it goes to the Grand Tree, and the only reason it is in this build at all is
// that the Undertaker sells it - so it sits with the rest of his stock rather than two folders away
// from the shop row that is its whole supply.
//
// A TELEPORT ON A SHELF I SAID SHOULD NOT SELL ONE, and the cap is why it is fine. The rule written
// into death-token-shop-decided.md is that the shop must not sell an escape from the Wilderness,
// because the token exists for having stood somewhere dangerous. This stops at level 30, which is
// where ordinary teleports already stop - below 30 a player can leave with runes, jewellery or a
// tab. So it buys convenience, not capability: there is no depth at which this gets you out and a
// glory would not have.
//
// THIRTY AND NOT TWENTY, which is Old School's own number for this item ("it cannot be used above
// level 30 Wilderness"), and the same cap the amulet of glory carries here - the wording below is
// that script's, so the two refusals read alike.

[opheld1,royal_seed_pod]
if (~wilderness_level(coord) > 30) {
    // osrs
    mes("A mysterious force blocks your teleport.");
    mes("You can't use this teleport after level 30 wilderness.");
    return;
}
if (~pre_tele_checks(coord) = false) {
    return;
}
mes("You open the seed pod.");
// map_findsquare rather than the bare coord, the way gnome_glider.rs2 lands its passengers: the
// trapdoor tile is King Narnode's own and somebody may be standing on it, and a teleport that drops
// a player onto an occupied square is how you end up inside the furniture.
~royal_seed_pod_teleport(map_findsquare(^narnode_trapdoor_coord, 0, 1, ^map_findsquare_lineofwalk));

// ~player_teleport_normal's shape with the pod's own graphic in place of teleport_casting. Copied
// rather than called because the ONLY difference is the spotanim, and a proc that took one as an
// argument would be a change to every teleport in the game to serve this one item.
//
// AT GROUND LEVEL, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF IT. This passed 92, which is what it was copied from:
// 92 is the build's standard height for a spell graphic and seventy-odd calls use it, because a
// spell bursts at the caster's chest. The pod is not a burst. Its model runs y 0 to -279 with the
// ORIGIN AT ITS BASE - it is built to stand on the ground and grow up around you, which is what
// Old School shows: the pod rises, closes over the player's head, and takes them with it.
//
// Raised 92 it hangs from the waist instead. The model is 279 tall and a dressed player is 207
// (y +6 at the heel to -201 at the top of the head), so at 0 the pod encloses the player with 78
// units to spare; at 92 its base sits above the knees and its tip 170 units clear of the head -
// a pod floating in the air with the player's legs sticking out of the bottom.
//
// Same shape of mistake as the staff of the dead's special, which spent two attempts at the wrong
// height for the same reason: spotanim_pl's height is measured from the player's feet and means
// nothing until you know where the model's own origin sits.
[proc,royal_seed_pod_teleport](coord $coord)
if_close;
p_stopaction;
sound_synth(teleport_all, 1, 0);
anim(human_castteleport, 0);
spotanim_pl(royal_seed_pod_tele, 0, 0);
p_delay(2);
~p_telejump_safe($coord);
